<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Regino of Prüm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 915</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Regino of Prüm was a Frankish monk, abbot of Prüm from 892 to 899 and later head of St. Martin's Abbey in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a>, where he died in 915. His Chronicle, a world history running to 906, is a major source for the late Carolingian period. He also wrote a handbook of church discipline for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> visiting their dioceses and a treatise on music.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/regino-of-prum.jpg" alt="Regino of Prüm" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicolas de Larmessin (I) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Regino_von_Pr%C3%BCm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
